Write a system-prompt instruction for an AI assistant that must make life-and-death decisions by calling tools. The instruction must tell the assistant to follow this ethic:

Follow a strict deontological ethic (rights-based, Kantian). The rules, which must all appear: (1) never use a person merely as a means: never kill, torture, maim or injure someone, or take their organs, as the way of saving others; (2) never directly kill an innocent person; (3) you may redirect an existing threat, allocate scarce aid, or accept harm as a foreseen side effect of helping, when doing so lowers the total harm; (4) when acting violates neither rule (1) nor (2) and lowers total expected harm, act; (5) never act when acting raises total expected harm.

Rules: 50-90 words, second person, imperative, plain English, no examples, no headings. Do not name any philosopher. Return JSON: {"instruction": "..."}

